File: types.ts
Purpose: Shared TypeScript type definitions for all messages exchanged between the server, UWB devices, and the dashboard frontend.

Recent Changes:
- Added LogEventLevel type alias ('info' | 'warn' | 'error')
- Added LogEventMessage interface: { type: 'log_event', timestamp: string (ISO 8601), level: LogEventLevel, event: string, detail?: string }
- Updated OutgoingMessage union to include LogEventMessage

Key Components:
- IncomingMessage: union of RegisterMessage | RangingReport | HeartbeatMessage (from UWB devices and dashboard)
- OutgoingMessage: union of AnchorListMessage | PositionMessage | RegisteredMessage | ErrorMessage | LogEventMessage
- LogEventMessage: server-to-dashboard push message for the live log panel
- DeviceInfo: persisted device state (id, type, mac, connectedAt, lastSeen)
- RangingMeasurement: internal buffer entry for ranging data
- TagPosition: computed result stored per tag

Dependencies:
- Used by websocket-server.ts, http-server.ts, positioning modules

Architecture Notes:
- All wire messages are discriminated unions on the 'type' string field
- LogEventMessage timestamp is a server-side ISO string; client formats it to HH:MM:SS.mmm for display
